From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Onyx contributors <onyx@localhost>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 23:58:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 12/18] [Onyx] WebCrypto on mbedTLS; PlatformPasteboard for
 Onyx

The WebCrypto back end of USE(MBEDTLS), on mbedTLS's classic API: HMAC, AES-CBC / CTR / GCM / KW /
CFB8, PBKDF2, HKDF, ECDSA and ECDH (P-256, P-384, P-521), RSASSA-PKCS1-v1_5, RSA-OAEP, RSA-PSS
(HAVE_RSA_PSS), the keys' raw / JWK / SPKI / PKCS#8 forms parsed and written here (mbedTLS's own
parser accepts more than WebCrypto allows, and it has no PKCS#8 writer). mbedTLS is built without
threading and its RSA / EC operations write into the context: every operation works on a private
copy of the key. RSA key generation runs on a work queue. The stubs
(CryptoNotImplementedMbedTLS.cpp) are gone.

PlatformPasteboard for PLATFORM(ONYX) beside USE(LIBWPE): an in-process clipboard (text and HTML)
until libonyxposix reaches the system's.
